{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>אשר</b> — HaShem is what is said, \"then they will say of you according to their plotting.\" And the word נשוא is a past-tense verb with an added alef, like \"ההלכוא אתו\"; כי means \"for,\" like \"ונשו את כלמתם.\"" "<b>ומלת עריך</b> — like \"your enemies,\" and the word אותך or שמך is missing. And R. Moses said: נשוא is a participle and עריך is a pronoun of שמך, like \"כי נאץ נאצת את אויבי ה'\"; if so, נשוא is a past-tense verb."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:16.744026526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}